{"id":"chatcmpl-dcbb30f1-ca66-4c16-97ab-7529a945fa61","object":"chat.completion","created":1795229993,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a strategy of recognizing when a single image view is insufficient to distinguish between lateralized findings, then delegating to a specialized expert tool for focused interpretation. The key insight is that ambiguous spatial information (left vs. right) on a lateral projection requires domain-specific reasoning about anatomical landmarks rather than generic visual inspection.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When a question requires distinguishing between lateralized (left/right) findings on a single projection that collapses depth, recognize the ambiguity and seek specialized interpretation rather than guessing.\",\n    \"Identify the imaging modality and projection first, then reason about which anatomical landmarks are visible and how pathology would manifest differently on each side.\",\n    \"Delegate to a domain-expert tool when standard visual reasoning cannot resolve a binary distinction that depends on subtle radiological signs.\",\n    \"Use known anatomical asymmetries (e.g., diaphragm height differences) as priors to constrain which side is more likely affected.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging interpretation\": \"Establish projection type and visible landmarks before reasoning; flag cases where a single view cannot resolve laterality and route to expert interpretation.\",\n    \"Binary classification under ambiguity\": \"When two options differ only by a spatial or contextual attribute not directly observable, use domain priors and expert tools to break the tie rather than defaulting to visual heuristics.\",\n    \"Tool-assisted reasoning\": \"Recognize when a specialized tool can supply the discriminating signal; formulate a focused query that asks for the specific features needed to distinguish the options.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the projection/view type and which anatomical landmarks are visible before committing to a lateralized answer.\",\n    \"Verify that the chosen answer is supported by a specific discriminating sign, not just general opacity, when options differ only by side.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":672,"total_tokens":1046,"completion_tokens":374,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":672},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":374}}}